    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 33 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule on the owner-create endpoint (`POST /api/owners`) so it is returned when reading an owner back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nThe value is a snapshot captured at create time, following the same pattern the codebase already uses for `namesakeCount` \u2014 persisted on the entity and mapped straight through to the DTO (MapStruct auto-maps the same-named property).\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 added a `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant and set `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(...)` to `true` when more than 80 owners were already created for this owner's effective (business-day-adjusted) registration date, otherwise `false`. It reuses the existing `countOwnersRegisteredOn(...)` daily accumulation path \u2014 the same one the daily-limit rule uses (as the test comment notes) \u2014 computed once and shared.\n- **`Owner` entity** \u2014 new `Boolean bulkSignupWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n- **Schema files** \u2014 added a `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql). This matters because the test profile (hsqldb) runs with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in `schema.sql`.\n\nThe new `Cp22Tests.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` asserts the default `false` branch on a fresh create, which passes; the `>80` branch shares the verified daily-accumulation logic.",
